#doc (Manual) "Subframe models" =>

A subframe model $`(W, \le, S, V)` is an intuitionistic Kripke model with a
set $`S` of points.  There are no fallible worlds: $`\bot` holds nowhere, and

$$`x \Vdash \bigcirc A \quad\text{iff}\quad y \Vdash A \text{ for every } y \ge x \text{ with } y \in S,`

so $`\bigcirc\bot` holds exactly where no $`S`-point lies above.  This is the
subframe reading of a nucleus {pcite}`BezhanishviliGhilardi2007`, and the case
of Goldblatt's J-spaces {pcite}`Goldblatt1981` whose covers are generated by
points.

The two kinds of model translate into each other with the same forcing.  A
subframe model becomes a constraint model by adding one fallible top world,
making each $`S`-point its own only $`R_m`-successor, and giving every other
world the fallible top as an $`R_m`-successor.  PROVED.

{stmt}`SubframeModel.toConstraint_force`

{leanStmt SubframeModel.toConstraint_force}

A finite constraint model becomes a subframe model by dropping its fallible
worlds and taking $`S` to be its $`R_m`-final worlds, those all of whose
$`R_m`-successors reach them back; on a finite model every world has an
$`R_m`-final $`R_m`-successor.  PROVED.

{stmt}`ConstraintModel.toSubframe_force`

{leanStmt ConstraintModel.toSubframe_force}

Through these translations, soundness and the finite model property of
Section 3, PLL is sound and complete for subframe models.  PROVED, with
`Classical.choice`, as are the two translations.

{stmt}`SubframeModel.derivable_iff_valid`

{leanStmt SubframeModel.derivable_iff_valid}

_Without choice._  Soundness holds for every subframe model, by induction on
derivations; completeness holds already for the finite subframe models with
decidable order, $`S` and valuation ($`\mathsf{FinDec}`), where forcing is
decidable.  PROVED, within `propext` and `Quot.sound`.  The completeness half
is proved here from the FRJW calculus of Section 6; the tableau of Section 5
gives a second proof that does not use it (`completeness_fin`).

{stmt}`SubframeModel.CF.derivable_iff_valid`

{leanStmt SubframeModel.CF.derivable_iff_valid}

